       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the standard maximum.\n2. **A lower starting dose**, such as 5 mg once daily, or 2.5 mg if the patient is frail or you want a cautious start.\n3. **30 mg as written**, if it's intentional. If so, please tell me the clinical rationale so I can add it to the order note. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n\nIt's also possible 30 mg was a typo, for example for 10 mg or 3.0 mg. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
